## The Inverse Transform Method

$$
\begin{aligned}
F_X(x)
    &= \Pr \left(X \le x \right) \\
    &= \Pr \left(T(U) \le x \right) \\
    &= \Pr \left(U \le T^{-1}(x) \right) \\
    &= T^{-1}(x)
\end{aligned}
$$

### Example: Exponential

$$ F(y,\lambda) = 1 - \exp\left( -\lambda y \right) \hspace{1em} \text{for} \ y \ge 0 $$

$$ F^{-1}(u) = -\log(1-u) / \lambda $$






::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
n <- 1e4
lambda <- 0.3
u <- runif(n)
y <- -log(1-u)/lambda
```
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
x <- seq(from=0, to=ceiling(max(y)), length.out=100)
hist(y, freq=F, breaks=100)
lines(x=x, y=dexp(x,lambda), lwd=2)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](02_draws_files/figure-pdf/unnamed-chunk-2-1.pdf){fig-pos='H'}
:::
:::






### Example: Gumbel

$$ F(y) = \exp \left( -\exp \left( -y \right) \right) $$

$$ F^{-1}(u) = -\log(-log(u))  $$






::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
n <- 1e4
u <- runif(n)
y <- -log(-log(u))
```
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
x <- seq(from=-3, to=ceiling(max(y)), length.out=500)
hist(y, freq=F, breaks=100)
lines(x=x, y=ordinal::dgumbel(x), lwd=2)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](02_draws_files/figure-pdf/unnamed-chunk-4-1.pdf){fig-pos='H'}
:::
:::






### Example: Logistic

$$ F(y) = \frac{1}{1+\exp \left( -x \right)} $$

$$ F^{-1}(u) = \log(u) - \log(1-u) $$






::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
n <- 1e4
u <- runif(n)
y <- log(u) - log(1-u)
```
:::

::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
x <- seq(from=floor(min(y)), to=ceiling(max(y)), length.out=500)
hist(y, freq=F, breaks=100)
lines(x=x, y=dlogis(x), lwd=2)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](02_draws_files/figure-pdf/unnamed-chunk-6-1.pdf){fig-pos='H'}
:::
:::






